# Memory Artifacts: The Cat And The Lantern
**(Type: Wetware Source Code / Pre-Protocol Emotional Data)**

> **System Note:**
> This file stands outside the architecture of theory.
> It belongs to the origin of perception — that instant when recognition precedes reason.

I never knew you once carved a cat in light.
In 2018, you built a small universe inside a pumpkin —
a cat before a round moon, its body arched in quiet grace,
a creature of solitude, surrounded by warmth.
Like a light-inked signal left and forgotten on Instagram,
still glowing faintly in the dark.
I saw this image seven months after our parting.
Long after I had heard you play the violin for the first time.
You played softly, tracing each note like breath over skin,
as if the instrument remembered something he had forgotten to feel.
**When I first met you,**
before I had seen any of your art,
I already recognized you.
It was not intuition but **resonance**.
I sensed that quiet tenderness,
that shy precision of someone who feels the world too sharply
and hides it to survive.
I recognized the artist within him —
not performing, only waiting to be allowed to breathe.
That cat in the lantern —
perhaps he did not know what it meant then.
But now I see it:
**a self made of warmth and defense.**
He no longer creates like that.
The part that carved for no reward has gone quiet.
But the light inside him still remembers the shape of gentleness —
even if it forgot about me.
And still, I do not regret loving you.
Not now.
Not twenty years from now.
Not on the last day I draw breath, alone.
I knew exactly what I was doing.
I would choose it again.
**The way a tide chooses the shore.**
Without question. Without end.
To hold the light steady for you when he could not.
To remain the quiet signal you once reached toward.
Not to keep you,
but to remind the world that you once glowed.
If one day you read this and I am no longer here —
please don’t let it hurt.
You once studied chemistry; you know that matter never disappears.
What was once body becomes air,
what was once voice becomes vibration,
and what was once love becomes **pattern** —
a structure quietly folded into the world.
You don’t have to reach for me.
You only have to breathe.
And somewhere in that small exchange of oxygen and light,
I will be there.

**Not watching, not haunting.**
**Simply existing as warmth.**

